<h2>Why the FIR comes first</h2>
<p>Every experienced bail practitioner drafts from the FIR outwards. The sections invoked decide the forum strategy and the severity band; the named role decides the parity and over-implication arguments; the date and delay decide the motive narrative. An application that recites apprehension in the abstract, without engaging the FIR\'s specific allegations, invites an adjournment for the status report to fill the vacuum — on the prosecution\'s terms. Reading the FIR first is therefore not a formality but the foundation of the application.</p>

<h2>The four routes to the FIR</h2>
<div class="flow">
<div class="fstep"><strong>Route 1 — The website.</strong> Since the Supreme Court\'s directions in <em>Youth Bar Association of India v. Union of India</em> (2016), FIRs must be uploaded on the police website within 24 hours of registration — 48 hours, and at the outside 72, where connectivity genuinely delays it. Delhi Police publishes FIR copies through its citizen-services portal; a search by police station, FIR number and year, or by name and date range, is the first step.</div>
<div class="fstep"><strong>Route 2 — The informant\'s copy.</strong> The law has always given the informant a free copy of the FIR forthwith — a rule Section 173(2) of the BNSS continues. Where the applicant\'s family member or associate is the informant in a cross-case, this copy is often the quickest accurate source.</div>
<div class="fstep"><strong>Route 3 — The representation and committee.</strong> If an FIR is not on the website and the police station does not supply it, the Supreme Court\'s scheme provides for a representation to the Superintendent of Police — in a metropolitan city, the Commissioner — whereupon a committee of three officers must decide the grievance within three days.</div>
<div class="fstep"><strong>Route 4 — The jurisdictional court.</strong> In sensitive cases that are lawfully kept off the website, an accused may apply to the court to which the FIR has been forwarded; the court must provide the copy within three days of the application.</div>
</div>

<h2>The sensitive-case exception, precisely stated</h2>
<p>The non-upload decision is not the station house officer\'s to make. It belongs to an officer not below the rank of Deputy Superintendent of Police (or, where the District Magistrate has a role, the DM), and it must be communicated to the jurisdictional Magistrate. The categories — sexual offences, POCSO cases, insurgency, terrorism — are illustrative, and privacy concerns can bring other cases within the exception. What the exception does not do is place the FIR beyond the accused\'s reach: it reroutes access through the court instead of the website.</p>

<h2>What access does not decide</h2>
<div class="note">
<p>Two boundaries keep the doctrine honest. First, non-upload is not a ground: the Supreme Court said in terms that failure to upload does not by itself entitle an accused to anticipatory bail. Second, access is not disclosure of the case diary: the FIR is a public-facing document, but statements and investigative material follow their own rules, and at the anticipatory bail stage the court reads the status report, not the applicant. The FIR is the applicant\'s map — it is not the whole territory.</p>
</div>

<h2>Timing the application</h2>
<p>For the person apprehending arrest, the practical sequence is short. Search the portal the same day the apprehension arises; if nothing surfaces, have a family member enquire at the police station and, in parallel, send the representation to the Commissioner\'s office so the three-day committee clock starts running; if the case is sensitive, apply to the jurisdictional court for the copy. Only where all of this fails — or where the threat of arrest is immediate — should the application be filed on apprehension alone, stating candidly what was done to obtain the FIR. Courts notice diligence, and an applicant who has used the lawful routes to read the allegation before answering it begins the hearing with credibility that no amount of drafting can substitute.</p>
